# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# agent-duet coordination artifacts
#
# A run writes these into the working tree it operates on. The coordinator archives
# and removes them before validation, and finalize refuses to commit them, but a
# failed or cancelled run can leave them behind — and this repository is itself a
# valid run target. Ignoring them keeps a crashed run from ever staging its scratch.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE_CRITIQUE_REQUEST.md
GPT_CRITIQUE_FOR_CLAUDE.md

# Review scratch dropped in by hand. Critiques are working notes, not deliverables:
# whatever they were right about belongs in the code and in a test, and whatever they
# were wrong about should not sit in the repository contradicting it.
GPT_CRITIQUE.md
CLAUDE_CRITIQUE.md
*_CRITIQUE.md
*_CRITIQUE_*.md
CRITIQUE*.md
BUILD_SPEC.md

# Files the test fixtures write when a fake agent is pointed at a real tree.
/impl.py
/test_impl.py

# Throwaway git indexes built by owned_tree_sha().
*.index
!*.index/

# Local state, config, and logs. These belong in ~/.local/state and ~/.config;
# a copy here would be machine-specific at best and credential-bearing at worst.
config.toml
state.sqlite3*
/runs/
/worktrees/
/logs/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python

# Packaging and build output
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
MANIFEST
pip-wheel-metadata/
share/python-wheels/

# Environments. This project installs into the interpreter that runs pip and does
# not use a virtualenv, but an accidental one must never be committed.
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
uv.lock

# Test, type, and lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
*.cover
nosetests.xml
junit*.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local overrides
#
# Nothing in this project reads a .env file, deliberately. These patterns exist so a
# stray one cannot be committed by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!**/prompts/*.md
secrets.*
credentials.*
*.credentials

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.sublime-*
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# Scratch and backups
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.old
/scratch/
/tmp/
